--TEST--
`isOpen` answers a plain `bool`, so "can I still use this connection" has two answers and not three — `rule:core-classes/db-one-api`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Db\Connection::isOpen
// The one member a closed connection still answers, which is why its return
// type matters: every other member of `Core\Db\Connection` throws a
// `LogicError` once the handle is released, and this one is what a caller asks
// so that it does not have to. A `?bool` would have added "the connection
// cannot say", and there is no such state — the handle is filed or it is not.
var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");

// The accepted reading, and the only one.
bool $state = $db->isOpen();

// And the boundary: the answer is a `bool` and not the connection, a name or a
// count, so nothing here is readable as anything a caller has to interpret.
string $wrong = $db->isOpen();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `bool`
   --> case.nvs:15:17
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
